the european commission presented its  long-awaited strategy for sustainable  and smart mobility according to it more  than 80 initiatives are to be launched  in the current legislative term  as socialists and democrats we are more  than welcoming this strategy  notably the revision of the co2  standards for cars  vans and trucks and the three million  public charging points  and thousand hydrogen filling stations  that should be in place by 2030  as well as the inclusion of shipping and  aviation  in the european trading system i am  happy to finally see  the long-awaited strategy for  sustainable and smart transport  we need to make all modes of transport  sustainable as soon as possible  and therefore i'm especially glad to see  that the strategy  includes proposal for sustainable fuels  in both  aviation and maritime with regards to  consumer rights  i'm also extremely happy to see that the  proposal  from us socialists and democrats on  creating a european travel guarantee  fund  is part of the strategy we cannot  continue to force  consumers to bail out airlines and  travel agents  however as socialist we would have liked  to see  stronger proposals on workers rights we  need to make sure  that the new strategy for the future of  transport also entails good working  condition  for all those working in transport and  we will continue  to push for concrete proposals from the  commission to improve working conditions  in transport finally i can promise that  we will make  our outmos to ensure that all proposals  and targets are ambitious  and implemented in due time to create a  sustainable  transport in the future
 

